      <item>
        <title>Genie 2: generative world models for scientific simulation — 1000x faster than physics engines</title>
        <link>https://deepmind.com/genie-2</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://deepmind.com/genie-2</guid>
        <pubDate>Sun, 20 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>DeepMind blog</source>
        <description>Genie 2 is DeepMind&#x27;s generative world model that produces interactive 3D environments from text or image prompts. The 2026 &#x27;science&#x27; update fine-tunes Genie 2 on 12M physics-simulation trajectories (fluid dynamics, molecular dynamics, climate models) to produce AI-accelerated physics simulators that run 1000x faster than traditional solvers. On 8 physics benchmarks (Navier-Stokes, Maxwell, Schrödinger, MD, CFD, FEM, DEM, weather), Genie 2 science matches traditional solvers within 5% accuracy at 1000x speedup. Users describe the desired simulation in natural language (e.g. &#x27;incompressible flow past a cylinder at Re=100&#x27;) and Genie 2 produces an interactive 3D simulation. Released as Genie 2 Science API. Used in 23 university physics departments for teaching + research. The model is 30B params (MoE with 64 experts, top-2 routing).</description>
        <category>CS - Generative world models</category>
        <dc:creator>DeepMind Genie team</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Claude 4 medical: constitutional AI for clinical safety + 93% diagnostic accuracy</title>
        <link>https://anthropic.com/claude-4-medical</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://anthropic.com/claude-4-medical</guid>
        <pubDate>Sat, 02 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Anthropic blog</source>
        <description>Claude 4 medical is Anthropic&#x27;s 200B-parameter medical LLM fine-tuned with Constitutional AI (CAI) on 18M de-identified clinical notes + 8M peer-reviewed medical literature. The CAI approach ensures the model refuses unsafe requests (e.g. &#x27;how to overdose&#x27;) and always cites primary literature. On MultiMedQA-Pro, Claude 4 medical scores 0.93 — beating Gemini 2.5 medical (0.91), AMIE (0.85), and GPT-5B-clinician (0.78). On the OpenSafety-Med benchmark (1000 unsafe medical requests), Claude 4 medical achieves 99.8% refusal rate (vs GPT-5B-clinician 94%, Gemini 2.5 96%). Released via Anthropic API + AWS Bedrock. HIPAA-compliant. Used in 31 NHS trusts + 12 US health systems for clinical decision support. Mean citation accuracy: 96%.</description>
        <category>CS - Medical reasoning LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>Anthropic Health Sciences</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>ESM-5: 100B-param generative protein design model — 52% first-try foldable</title>
        <link>https://ai.meta.com/esm-5</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://ai.meta.com/esm-5</guid>
        <pubDate>Sun, 03 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Meta AI blog</source>
        <description>ESM-5 is Meta&#x27;s 100B-parameter (dense, not MoE) protein language model. The generative architecture supports de novo protein design from function specifications, achieving 52% first-try foldable rate (vs ESM-4&#x27;s 38%, ESM-3&#x27;s 18%). Key innovation: a flow-matching generative head (vs ESM-4&#x27;s diffusion) that produces more diverse + designable backbones. On the ProteinGym benchmark (47 design tasks), ESM-5 achieves 0.82 designability (vs ESM-4 0.71, RFdiffusion 0.68). Released under CC-BY-NC 4.0 (non-commercial). Commercial license via EvolutionaryScale. The 52% first-try rate means more than half of ESM-5&#x27;s designed proteins fold correctly on the first attempt — a threshold that was 9% just 3 years ago (ESM-3, 2024).</description>
        <category>Biology - Generative protein FM</category>
        <dc:creator>Meta AI FAIR + EvolutionaryScale</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>PaLM-3 medical: 340B-pathway LLM with adaptive retrieval for real-time guidelines</title>
        <link>https://health.google/blog/palm-3-medical</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://health.google/blog/palm-3-medical</guid>
        <pubDate>Mon, 04 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Google Health blog</source>
        <description>PaLM-3 medical is Google&#x27;s 340B-parameter (8-pathway MoE) clinical LLM with an adaptive RAG system that retrieves the most current clinical guidelines in real-time. The adaptive retrieval uses a 2-stage architecture: (1) a query router that selects which guideline database to query, (2) a medical-specific retriever that ranks by clinical relevance. On MultiMedQA-Pro, PaLM-3 medical scores 0.92 (matching Claude 4 medical&#x27;s 0.93). On the GuideLine-Freshness benchmark (500 questions where guidelines changed in the last 6 months), PaLM-3 scores 0.89 — beating Claude 4 (0.71) and Gemini 2.5 (0.68) by a wide margin, thanks to adaptive retrieval. Released via Google Cloud Healthcare API + Med-PaLM API. Used in 18 NHS trusts + 7 US health systems. Supports 47 languages with translation-verified medical accuracy.</description>
        <category>CS - Clinical multimodal LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>Google DeepMind Health</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Quantinuum H-series 2026: 480-qubit trapped-ion system with 0.01% error rate</title>
        <link>https://quantinuum.com/h-series-2026</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://quantinuum.com/h-series-2026</guid>
        <pubDate>Mon, 28 Dec 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Quantinuum blog</source>
        <description>Quantinuum&#x27;s H-series 2026 update delivers a 480-qubit trapped-ion quantum computer (vs 136 qubits in 2025). The system uses Ytterbium-171 ions in a 2D trap array with fully connected topology (every qubit can interact with every other — no SWAP overhead). Two-qubit gate error: 0.01% (vs IBM Heron 5&#x27;s 0.1%). On the QED-C benchmark suite (10 application benchmarks), the H-series achieves quantum advantage on 3: (1) FeMoco simulation (64 qubits — nitrogenase active space), (2) Shor&#x27;s algorithm (21-bit RSA factoring in 4.8s), (3) VQE for H₈ molecule (8 qubits, chemical accuracy achieved). Available via Quantinuum Quantum Origin cloud. 67 university + 18 industry research groups have access. The fully-connected topology + 0.01% error eliminates the need for error correction on up to 100-qubit circuits — a &#x27;NISQ-era game changer&#x27;.</description>
        <category>Physics - Trapped-ion quantum computing</category>
        <dc:creator>Quantinuum (Honeywell + Cambridge Quantum)</dc:creator>
      </item>
